        "original_id": "da2b16da-fcef-5697-8666-ea5ea50c1966",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Ehrlichman, Richard Nixon\n- Products: The Company, Washington: Behind Closed Doors\n- Concepts: Roman à clef, political fiction\n- Organizations: Simon & Schuster, Nixon administration, Watergate scandal\n\nFacts:\n- Roman à clef is French for “novel with a key” and refers to a novel that depicts real life behind a façade of fiction.\n- In 1976, Simon & Schuster first published The Company.\n- The Company is a political fiction roman à clef novel written by John Ehrlichman.\n- John Ehrlichman was a close aide to President Richard Nixon and was a figure in the Watergate scandal.\n- The Company was inspired by John Ehrlichman’s time in the Nixon administration.\n- Washington: Behind Closed Doors is based on John Ehrlichman’s book The Company.",
